\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\title{A commutator square on the torus}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{Let #{k} be a commutative unital ring, let #{d\ge 1} and
#{N\ge 1}, and write #{X=(\mathbb{Z}/N\mathbb{Z})^d}. The
operator #{D} is the counting operator #{d+d^\dagger} of
\ref{fdip-00OL}, on the cellular cochains of \ref{fdip-00OK}.
A vertex function #{f} acts on a cochain by the value at the
base vertex of the cube,
##{(f\cdot\alpha)(c_I(x))=f(x)\,\alpha(c_I(x)).}
This is the front-face rule of \ref{fdip-0093}, read at the base
vertex of a cube.}

\p{Write #{a_i(x)=f(x+\varepsilon_i)-f(x)}. When these differences
are constant, the square of the commutator is multiplication by
minus their sum of squares. When the mixed differences vanish,
the same square is still a multiplication, and the factor on a
vertex is read one step backward. The odd and even vectors of
each axis then compare #{D} with the centered operator and with
the Wilson operator, and the degree sign anticommutes with
#{D}.}

